WebGPU: anisotropy only with linear filters

WebGPU rejects a sampler with maxAnisotropy above 1 unless its minification, magnification and mip filters are all
linear. bgfx turned anisotropy off only when both the minification and magnification filters were point, so a
sampler with point mips, such as a shadow map's comparison sampler, was invalid, and so was every bind group and
command buffer using it.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
index 3a4cf85..ee335aa 100644
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -5783,9 +5783,11 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 
 		WGPUSampler sampler = s_renderWGPU->m_samplerStateCache.find(key);
 
-		const bool disableAniso = true
-			&& (BGFX_SAMPLER_MIN_POINT == (samplerFlags&BGFX_SAMPLER_MIN_POINT) )
-			&& (BGFX_SAMPLER_MAG_POINT == (samplerFlags&BGFX_SAMPLER_MAG_POINT) )
+		// WebGPU takes anisotropy only with linear minification, magnification and mip filters.
+		const bool disableAniso = false
+			|| (BGFX_SAMPLER_MIN_POINT == (samplerFlags&BGFX_SAMPLER_MIN_MASK) )
+			|| (BGFX_SAMPLER_MAG_POINT == (samplerFlags&BGFX_SAMPLER_MAG_MASK) )
+			|| (BGFX_SAMPLER_MIP_POINT == (samplerFlags&BGFX_SAMPLER_MIP_MASK) )
 			;
 
 		if (NULL == sampler)
